# accordion.zd — disclosure, from the browser.
#
# The one widget in this directory that is *complete*, and it is complete
# because the language already has the element that does it. §16.3.6's note
# on `Details` is the whole story: a `details` is focusable and operable
# from the keyboard with no handler, is announced as expanded or collapsed,
# expands when find-in-page lands inside it, and prints open. A disclosure
# hand-rolled out of a `Truth` and an `if` — which is what every program
# without this file writes — gets none of those. `expanded is …` now
# reaches `aria-expanded`, so such a thing could at least announce itself;
# it would still not be find-in-page-expandable, not printed open, and not
# operable without a handler. Nothing here writes `expanded`: a second
# `aria-expanded` beside the one the user agent maintains on the summary
# is how the two come to disagree.
#
# So this file is thin on purpose. It is two components, and their value is
# that they are the two shapes an accordion has, named, so that a program
# reaches for `Details` instead of for a signal.

# The container. It exists so the group has one place to be styled and one
# place to be read as a group, and for no other reason: it adds no
# behaviour, because the behaviour belongs to each section.
component Accordion with class, children
    Column class is class
        children

# One section: a summary that is always shown, and a body the reader opens.
#
# `title` is required because §16.3.6 requires `Summary` to be the first
# child of a `Details` — a `details` with no summary is labelled with
# whatever word the browser chose, in whatever language it chose it in.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO: the sections are independent, so opening one does
# not close the others. HTML has an answer — `name` on a `details` makes a
# set of them exclusive — and it is not an argument the vocabulary has, so
# there is no way to ask for it from here. Doing it with a signal instead
# would mean giving up `Details` and with it everything listed above, which
# is a bad trade for one behaviour.
component AccordionSection with title, class, children
    Details class is class
        Summary title
        children
